|* Post-layout sampler_core (whole composed cell), FLOATING substrate, rings
|* 2-4 PRESENT BUT STOPPED (en2/en3/en4 held at 0 for the whole run) -- the
|* sampler_core-scope sibling of
|* sim/post-layout-ro-array-core/testbench/tb_post_layout_ro_array_core_substrate_float_solo.spice,
|* now with all six sampler_dff instances present, loaded and clocked
|* identically to the sibling _float and _tied decks (the tied deck being
|* sim/post-layout-sampler-core/testbench/tb_post_layout_sampler_core.spice's
|* own post-layout half, already run and recorded).
|*
|* Purpose: separate LOADING (the floating node's own capacitance/impedance,
|* plus everything on it that is common to all three decks) from COUPLING
|* (ring 1's period moving because rings 2-4 are actually driving the same
|* shared node), the same three-way decomposition DR-0005 (ring scope) and
|* DR-0006 (array scope) used:
|*
|*   loading  = t(this deck)                              - t(tied)
|*   coupling = t(substrate_float, all 4 rings running)    - t(this deck)
|*
|* Holding the six samplers' own clk/rst_n stimulus IDENTICAL across
|* TIED/FLOAT/SOLO (rather than omitting them here) means their own
|* contribution to substrate loading is common to all three decks and
|* cancels out of BOTH differences above -- what changes between this deck
|* and the sibling _float deck is only whether rings 2-4 are switching,
|* isolating the ring-to-ring term DR-0003 section 8 actually asks about.
|*
|* Same sampler_core_pex extraction as the sibling _tied/_float decks in
|* this directory (real physical ring/buffer/xor2/sampler-bank proximity,
|* not leaf cells hand-tied to a shared node), so this is the strongest
|* available bound on the substrate mechanism this repo has produced at
|* sampler_core scope -- still not the physical answer (the extractor emits
|* no substrate or tap resistance at all; klayout-tools#1503), but bracketing
|* the terminals of a real, physically-placed layout's own shared node.
|*
|* With en2/en3/en4 held at 0, ro_nand2's own defined-output-on-disable state
|* (design/README.md; DR-0003) pins ring2/3/4's node ro_ring5 outputs high --
|* a defined, non-switching state, not a floating one -- so rn2/rn3/rn4 (and
|* therefore ro2/ro3/ro4 and the XOR tree downstream of them) settle and stay
|* put; only ring 1 free-runs. The six samplers still latch whatever settles
|* onto their own `d` pins at each clk edge -- a defined value, not floating
|* -- so this deck's own reset/capture behaviour is not separately measured
|* (that is the sibling _tied deck's own scope); only ring 1's period and the
|* substrate node's own swing are read here.
|*
|* TWO measurement windows, matching the sibling _float deck exactly (see
|* that deck's header for the full statement). `p_tr1` (rise=3 -> rise=13)
|* is the tied deck's own estimator verbatim and, at this design's
|* post-layout ring periods, falls entirely before `rst_n` releases at
|* 300 ns -- samplers loaded and placed, not switching. `p_tr1_clk` is a
|* ten-period average taken from the first rising edge past 400 ns, inside
|* the clocked window, with all six samplers actually latching; it is
|* time-gated (`TRIG`/`TARG ... TD=400n`) rather than rise-indexed because
|* the ring period varies 3.1x across this repo's PVT grid. Only the
|* `coupling` half of the decomposition can be computed on the clocked
|* estimator, since the already-minted tied records carry no counterpart to
|* it.
|*
|* Global substrate addressing, corrected from the start (see the sibling
|* _float deck's header for DR-0006's own documented `v(xarr.vsubs)` defect
|* this deck avoids): `vsubs` is `.global`, addressed as `v(vsubs)`.
|*
|* This file is a TEMPLATE: sim/bin/corner-run.py substitutes /Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice,
|* ff, -40.0, 1.98 and 5p. As committed it is not a
|* runnable deck. Invoke with
|* `--pex-lib layout/pex-sampler-core/sampler_core_pex.spice`.
|
|.option scale=1u
|.lib "/Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice" ff
|
|.include "/Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex-sampler-core/sampler_core_pex.spice"
|
|.temp -40.0
|
|* --- substrate return node: FLOATING (see header) -- no Vsub source ----
|
|Vddrp1 pvddr1 0 dc 1.98
|Vddrp2 pvddr2 0 dc 1.98
|Vddrp3 pvddr3 0 dc 1.98
|Vddrp4 pvddr4 0 dc 1.98
|Vddp pvdd 0 dc 1.98
|Venp1 pen1 0 PULSE(0 1.98 5n 100p 100p 1u 2u)
|* rings 2-4: held at 0 for the whole run -- present, but never released.
|Venp2 pen2 0 dc 0
|Venp3 pen3 0 dc 0
|Venp4 pen4 0 dc 0
|Vrstnp prst_n 0 PULSE(0 1.98 300n 100p 100p 10u 20u)
|Vclkp pclk 0 PULSE(0 1.98 320n 100p 100p 49.8n 100n)
|xarr pen1 pen2 pen3 pen4 pvddr1 pvddr2 pvddr3 pvddr4 pvdd 0 pclk prst_n
|+ praw_bit praw_valid pring_bit1 pring_bit2 pring_bit3 pring_bit4
|+ sampler_core_pex
|
|.ic v(xarr.ro1)=0 v(xarr.ro2)=0 v(xarr.ro3)=0 v(xarr.ro4)=0
|
|.save v(xarr.ro1) v(vsubs)
|
|* tstop is 600 ns, not the tied deck's 800 ns -- see the sibling _float
|* deck's own note on the same line for why that truncation is provably
|* immaterial to every number either deck reports.
|.tran 5p 600n uic
|
|.control
|run
|
|* --- primary estimator: identical to the tied and _float decks ---------
|meas tran pt1a when v(xarr.ro1)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran pt1b when v(xarr.ro1)=0.5*1.98 rise=13
|let p_tr1 = (pt1b - pt1a)/10
|
|* --- second estimator: clocked window, time-gated (see header) ---------
|meas tran pd1_clk TRIG v(xarr.ro1) VAL=0.5*1.98 RISE=1 TD=400n
|+ TARG v(xarr.ro1) VAL=0.5*1.98 RISE=11 TD=400n
|let p_tr1_clk = pd1_clk/10
|
|* --- shared substrate node's own excursion, two windows ----------------
|meas tran vsub_rst_max MAX v(vsubs) from=100n to=300n
|meas tran vsub_rst_min MIN v(vsubs) from=100n to=300n
|let vsub_swing_rst = (vsub_rst_max - vsub_rst_min) / 1.98
|meas tran vsub_clk_max MAX v(vsubs) from=400n to=600n
|meas tran vsub_clk_min MIN v(vsubs) from=400n to=600n
|let vsub_swing_clk = (vsub_clk_max - vsub_clk_min) / 1.98
|
|print p_tr1
|print p_tr1_clk
|print vsub_swing_rst
|print vsub_swing_clk
|.endc
|.end
|

